From 25db3c530484ac486d81e13ce0d3445ddf0d4b45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:02:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app,ui): built-in 5-axis self-centering vises, centred
 on the stock

Self-centering vises at 52, 75, 80 and 125 mm jaw width ride #788's
built-in vise as a style (`ViseStyle::SelfCentering`): both jaws close on
the centre, so "Fit to the stock" centres the vise on the stock and
closes the jaws to its width within the clamping range. The geometry is
one generated closed shell (body, two jaw bodies, an optional dovetail
lip drawn solid). Nonsense figures, stock outside the clamping range and
stock off the vise's centre are refused by name. Placing and editing are
the existing InsertVise / SetVise (one undo each); the project file takes
an optional `self_centering` key; MCP `add_builtin_vise` / `set_vise`
list the sizes and take min_opening / lip_height / lip_depth; the dialog
shows the sizes in their own row with their own fields.

Tilted setups: the placed vise is judged by the posed mesh laws - a tool
leaning into a jaw is struck where the same tip upright clears it, the
same lean from the centre clears, and a 3+2 face over the clamped stock
posts until the jaws are raised into it.

Fixes #787

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
